---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
const SIZES = [10, 100, 1000, 10000, 100000, 1000000];
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="A dynamic array that starts with room for 1 item and is resized when full. The cost counted is element copies. Time is an assumption of one nanosecond per copy; nothing is timed on your machine.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>With <b>Growth policy</b> "Double" and <b>Number of appends</b> at <b>100,000</b>: <b>131,071</b> copies in total, <b>1.31</b> per append, so the average is tiny. But the worst single append copies <b>65,536</b> elements, about <b>65.5</b> µs, and the chart shows 17 spikes.</li>
    <li>Switch <b>Growth policy</b> to "Add 10 slots": the total explodes to <b>499,960,000</b> copies, <b>4,999.60</b> per append. Growing by a constant is not amortized O(1). Switch to "Grow by 1.5x" for <b>276,521</b> copies, <b>2.76</b> per append.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Growth policy</b> back to "Double" and <b>Number of appends</b> to <b>1,000</b>: <b>1,023</b> copies, and the worst append is <b>512</b> copies.</li>
    <li>In the shrink box, set <b>Shrink when size drops to</b> "1/2 of capacity", with <b>Items in the array</b> at <b>1,025</b> and <b>Remove-and-append cycles</b> at <b>100</b>: every cycle shrinks and regrows the array, <b>204,800</b> copies in all. Choose "1/4 of capacity" and it falls to 0.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg am" data-am>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Growth policy <select class="pg-in" data-policy><option value="double" selected>Double</option><option value="x1.5">Grow by 1.5x</option><option value="add10">Add 10 slots</option></select></label>
      <label>Number of appends <select class="pg-in" data-n>{SIZES.map((n) => <option value={n} selected={n === 100000}>{n.toLocaleString('en-US')}</option>)}</select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Total copies</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-total></span><span class="pg-note" data-resizes></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-avgbox><h3>Average per append</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-avg></span><span class="pg-note">total copies divided by appends</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-worstbox><h3>Worst single append</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-worst></span><span class="pg-note" data-worstnote></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>Copies made by each append, over time</h3>
      <svg class="am-chart" data-chart viewBox="0 0 600 120" preserveAspectRatio="none" role="img" aria-label="Copies per append over time"></svg>
      <span class="pg-note" data-axis></span>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict role="status"></p>
    <h3 class="am-h">Shrinking too eagerly</h3>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Shrink when size drops to <select class="pg-in" data-rule><option value="never">Never shrink</option><option value="half" selected>1/2 of capacity</option><option value="quarter">1/4 of capacity</option></select></label>
      <label>Items in the array <select class="pg-in" data-items><option value="65">65</option><option value="1025" selected>1,025</option><option value="16385">16,385</option></select></label>
      <label>Remove-and-append cycles <select class="pg-in" data-cycles><option value="10">10</option><option value="100" selected>100</option><option value="1000">1,000</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-tbox><h3>Copies in the cycles</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-tcopies></span><span class="pg-note" data-tnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-3)"><h3>Per cycle</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-tper></span><span class="pg-note" data-ttime></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-note">Assumptions: capacity starts at 1; "Double" doubles it, "Grow by 1.5x" adds half (at least 1), "Add 10 slots" adds 10. Only the copies made while resizing are counted, plus nothing for the write itself. One copy takes 1 ns, with no cache or allocator cost. In the shrink test the array starts just past a power of two, so its capacity is about twice its size, then each cycle removes one item and appends one; shrinking halves the capacity. Real runtimes use their own growth factors, commonly between about 1.125x and 2x.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, formatThousands, formatOneDecimalBelow100 } from '../playground';
  const POLICIES: Record<string, (cap: number) => number> = {
    double: (cap) => cap * 2,
    'x1.5': (cap) => Math.max(cap + 1, cap + Math.floor(cap / 2)),
    add10: (cap) => cap + 10,
  };
  const NS_PER_COPY = 1;
  const BUCKETS = 150;
  // Same model as the code samples.
  function appendMany(policy: string, n: number) {
    let cap = 1, size = 0, total = 0, worst = 0, resizes = 0;
    const events: [number, number][] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      let copies = 0;
      if (size === cap) { copies = size; cap = POLICIES[policy](cap); resizes++; events.push([i, copies]); }
      size++;
      total += copies;
      if (copies > worst) worst = copies;
    }
    return { total, worst, resizes, events };
  }
  function thrash(rule: string, items: number, cycles: number): number {
    const div = ({ never: 0, half: 2, quarter: 4 } as Record<string, number>)[rule];
    let cap = 1;
    while (cap < items) cap *= 2;
    let size = items, copies = 0;
    for (let c = 0; c < cycles; c++) {
      size--;
      if (div > 0 && size * div <= cap) { copies += size; cap = cap / 2; }
      if (size === cap) { copies += size; cap *= 2; }
      size++;
    }
    return copies;
  }
  function fmt2(total: number, n: number): string {
    const hundredths = Math.floor((total * 100) / n);
    return `${formatThousands(Math.floor(hundredths / 100))}.${String(hundredths % 100).padStart(2, '0')}`;
  }
  function timeText(copies: number): string {
    const ns = copies * NS_PER_COPY;
    if (ns < 1000) return `${formatThousands(ns)} ns`;
    if (ns < 1e6) return `${formatOneDecimalBelow100(ns / 1e3)} µs`;
    if (ns < 1e9) return `${formatOneDecimalBelow100(ns / 1e6)} ms`;
    return `${formatOneDecimalBelow100(ns / 1e9)} s`;
  }

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-am]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const val = (s: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(s).value;
    const SVG = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
    function draw() {
      const policy = val('[data-policy]'), n = Number(val('[data-n]'));
      const r = appendMany(policy, n);
      q('[data-total]').textContent = formatThousands(r.total);
      q('[data-resizes]').textContent = `${formatThousands(r.resizes)} resize${r.resizes === 1 ? '' : 's'} in ${formatThousands(n)} appends`;
      q('[data-avg]').textContent = fmt2(r.total, n);
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-avgbox]').style.setProperty('--c', r.total / n < 5 ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q('[data-worst]').textContent = `${formatThousands(r.worst)} copies`;
      q('[data-worstnote]').textContent = `about ${timeText(r.worst)} at 1 ns per copy, all in one append`;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-worstbox]').style.setProperty('--c', r.worst > 1000 ? 'var(--signal)' : 'var(--good)');
      // Chart: the largest cost inside each slice of the sequence, so a spike is never averaged away.
      const chart = q<SVGElement>('[data-chart]');
      chart.textContent = '';
      const per = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(n / BUCKETS));
      const nb = Math.ceil(n / per);
      const max = new Array<number>(nb).fill(0);
      for (const [i, c] of r.events) { const b = Math.floor(i / per); if (c > max[b]) max[b] = c; }
      const peak = Math.max(1, r.worst);
      const w = 600 / nb;
      max.forEach((v, b) => {
        const rect = document.createElementNS(SVG, 'rect');
        const h = v === 0 ? 1 : Math.max(2, (v / peak) * 118);
        rect.setAttribute('x', String(b * w)); rect.setAttribute('width', String(Math.max(1, w - 0.5)));
        rect.setAttribute('y', String(120 - h)); rect.setAttribute('height', String(h));
        rect.setAttribute('fill', v === 0 ? 'var(--muted)' : 'var(--signal)');
        chart.appendChild(rect);
      });
      q('[data-axis]').textContent = `Left to right: append 1 to ${formatThousands(n)}, each column the largest cost in ${formatThousands(per)} append${per === 1 ? '' : 's'}. The tallest column is ${formatThousands(r.worst)} copies; grey columns are appends that copied nothing.`;
      q('[data-verdict]').textContent = r.total / n < 5
        ? `The average stays near ${fmt2(r.total, n)} copies per append, but one append copies ${formatThousands(r.worst)} elements.`
        : `Every append now averages ${fmt2(r.total, n)} copies: growing by a constant makes each append cost O(n) on average.`;
      // Shrink test.
      const t = thrash(val('[data-rule]'), Number(val('[data-items]')), Number(val('[data-cycles]')));
      const cycles = Number(val('[data-cycles]'));
      q('[data-tcopies]').textContent = formatThousands(t);
      q('[data-tnote]').textContent = t === 0 ? 'the array never resizes: there is slack on both sides of the boundary' : 'the array shrinks and grows again on every cycle (thrashing)';
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-tbox]').style.setProperty('--c', t === 0 ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q('[data-tper]').textContent = formatThousands(t / cycles);
      q('[data-ttime]').textContent = `copies per cycle, about ${timeText(t / cycles)} for each remove and append at 1 ns per copy`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .am-chart { width: 100%; height: 130px; display: block; background: var(--surface); border-radius: 6px; }
  .playground .am-h { margin: 14px 0 4px; font-size: 1rem; }
</style>
